  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1241 PM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nMonday night - Sunday\n\nUpper-lvl ridge will continue to build over the region, keeping \nnorthwest flow, dry conditions, and high temps in the low 90s \nthrough Wednesday. With ongoing drought conditions and RH values (%) \nin the mid-20s, a \"Limited\" fire danger will continue over northern \nparts of the area. Continue to heed any local burn bans and be \ncautious of outdoor burning. As the ridge migrates eastward mid-\nweek, southerly flow will push moisture into the area, easing fire \nweather concerns and increasing RH values through the weekend. \n\nAn upper-lvl low from the Southwest region and the absorbed remnants \nof Hurricane Polo will push a frontal boundary towards the region. \nRain chances will return as the frontal boundary approaches \nFriday, lasting through the weekend. Although hazardous weather is\nnot expected, forecast trends will be monitored as the week \nprogress. 50- 75% probability for rain are expected with the high \nprobability on Sunday (60-75% areawide). WPC estimates rainfall \ntotals of 2-4 inches over the weekend, which would help improve \nongoing drought conditions. /SW/",
